  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>On plotting the diagram of the given data we get,</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0070_70e338acb83a.png\" style=\"width: 249px; height: 210px;\" /></p><p>Now given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>On solving we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Now height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Distance of point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;to origin,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is an equilateral triangle,</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><msup><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>60</mn><mrow><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mn>60</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So, Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
